{"name":"Tapioca","hex":"#dac9b9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tapioca","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A starchy food made from the cassava plant, used in puddings.","The cassava plant, Manihot esculenta, from which tapioca is derived; manioc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tapioca"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tapioca","blocks":[{"text":"Tapioca is a starch extracted from the tubers of the cassava plant, a species native to the North and Northeast regions of Brazil, but which is now found in West Africa, Southeast Asia, and elsewhere. It is a perennial shrub adapted to the hot conditions of tropical lowlands. Cassava copes better with poor soils than many other food plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Tepung_casava.jpg/330px-Tepung_casava.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tapioca"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Manihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg/500px-Manihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Manihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg/1280px-Manihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Manihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg/500px-Manihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cassava tubers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManihot_esculenta_dsc07325.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Biji_delima_pacar_china.JPG/500px-Biji_delima_pacar_china.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Biji_delima_pacar_china.JPG/1280px-Biji_delima_